# Build-context whitelist for the MCP HTTP server image.
#
# Everything is excluded by default; only the runtime module graph is
# re-included below. This guarantees that local credential files (.env*,
# tokens, PEM keys), the dependency tree, and repository history can never
# enter the Docker build context, even if they are present in the working
# tree at build time. The explicit negative patterns at the end are defense
# in depth against a future re-inclusion mistake.

*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!config.js
!index.js
!outlook-auth-server.js
!bin/
!auth/
!calendar/
!email/
!folder/
!onedrive/
!power-automate/
!remote/
!rules/
!runtime/
!signature/
!sites/
!teams/
!utils/

# Defense in depth: never build with dependency trees, history, or secrets.
node_modules/
.git/
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.cert
*.token.json
vault-token.json
.outlook-mcp-tokens.json
vault-token.json*
